{
  "status": "Final representative rendered-pixel audit after ivory secondary ink and local carbon status fields; bounded to the recorded captures and projection.",
  "method": "Sharp decodes native 1440×900 JPEGs to raw RGB, without resizing. Foreground is the median luminance of the brightest 5% of a tight text ROI (97.5th percentile); nearby blank-screen background is its median luminance. sRGB linearization and 0.2126/0.7152/0.0722 weights give (Ltext+0.05)/(Lbackground+0.05). 95th/99th foreground-percentile ratios show antialiasing sensitivity.",
  "coordinates": "[x,y,width,height], native screenshot pixels",
  "limitations": [
    "Approximate rendered-pixel checks, not a complete WCAG determination. Small text often projects to 5–8 pixels high, leaving few fully covered glyph pixels; JPEG antialiasing, perspective and mip filtering limit interpretation.",
    "Nearby blank-background samples can differ from the exact background under glyphs across gradients. These estimates cannot certify every pixel or other viewport/animation state.",
    "The contact-hover capture highlights the main Contact display. contact-social-focus captures real keyboard focus on GitHub; its ROIs are shifted for the captured camera view. LinkedIn focus and other viewport sizes are not independently sampled.",
    "Tiny passive COM /02 and COM /03 equipment indices still have limited pixel contrast at this projection; they are not the functional link labels. This audit does not claim every small decorative pixel reaches 4.5:1.",
    "Hover subtitle glyph-core estimates are close to the 4.5:1 boundary: Case 4.62:1 and Contact 4.60:1; their 95th-percentile sensitivity estimates are 4.48:1 and 4.46:1. These small projected labels warrant checking again after camera, texture, lighting, or viewport changes.",
    "Projects focus was verified as DOM focus-visible by the capturing agent. Its text ROI excludes the focus rim.",
    "No font, geometry, lighting or animation changes were made by this audit."
  ],
